 Springboot - The extension of the larger Spring Framework, designed to simplify the development process by providing a streamlined way to configure and deploy applications. 
 
 Inversion of Control is a design principle where the control of object creation and dependency management is shifted (inverted) from the application code to the framework (like Spring).

Normally:
Your class creates its own dependencies.

With IoC:
The framework provides dependencies to your class.


When Spring starts the application, it scans for components.
For any class marked with @Component, Spring creates an object (a bean).
If any @Autowired field/constructor/setter is found, Spring:
Finds a matching bean from the context
Injects it automatically

@Id declares id as the primary key.
@GeneratedValue(...) tells JPA how to generate the value for this key.
GenerationType.AUTO (default)

@Entity
public class User {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;
    private String name;
}



